  "feature_instruction": "This `shared-backend` feature provides foundational utilities for the Spring Boot application, including a catch-all controller for client-side routing, a global exception handler, a custom resource not found exception, a standardized error response DTO, and a data seeder for initial database population. \n\n`SpaController.java` is responsible for forwarding all unhandled frontend routes to `index.html`, ensuring that client-side routing works correctly for the React SPA. It uses `@RequestMapping(\"/{path:[^\\\\.]*}\")` to catch any path that does not contain a file extension, effectively serving the single-page application.\n\n`GlobalExceptionHandler.java` is an `@ControllerAdvice` that centralizes exception handling across all `@Controller` components. It defines methods to handle specific exceptions, such as `ResourceNotFoundException`, and maps them to a consistent `ErrorResponse` DTO, ensuring a uniform error structure for the API consumers. It will catch `ResourceNotFoundException` and return an `ErrorResponse` with HTTP status 404 (Not Found).\n\n`ResourceNotFoundException.java` is a custom unchecked exception that should be thrown by service layers when a requested entity (e.g., a `MenuItem`, `Event`, or `Testimonial`) cannot be found in the database. It extends `RuntimeException` and takes a message as a constructor argument.\n\n`ErrorResponse.java` is a simple DTO used by `GlobalExceptionHandler` to structure error messages returned to the client. It contains fields for a timestamp, HTTP status, error message, and the path of the request that caused the error.\n\n`DataSeeder.java` is an `@Component` that implements `CommandLineRunner`. It is responsible for populating the database with initial data for `MenuItem`, `Event`, and `Testimonial` entities upon application startup. It injects `MenuItemRepository`, `EventRepository`, and `TestimonialRepository` to save predefined data. The `run` method will be executed once the application context is loaded. It should check if the repositories are empty before seeding to prevent duplicate data on subsequent application restarts.",
