  "feature_instruction": "The Reservation System feature manages customer table reservations for Circuit House. It consists of a `Reservation` entity and `ReservationStatus` enum, a `ReservationRepository` for persistence, a `ReservationService` for business logic, and two controllers: `ReservationController` for public-facing reservation creation and `AdminReservationController` for administrative management.\n\n### Reservation Entity and Status\n\n`Reservation.java` defines the core entity for a table reservation, including details like customer name, contact, date, time, party size, and its current `ReservationStatus`. `ReservationStatus.java` is an enum defining the possible states a reservation can be in (e.g., PENDING, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED, COMPLETED).\n\n### Persistence Layer\n\n`ReservationRepository.java` is a Spring Data JPA repository that provides standard CRUD operations for `Reservation` entities. It will also include custom query methods to find reservations by date, status, or customer.\n\n### Service Layer\n\n`ReservationService.java` encapsulates the business logic for reservations. It interacts with `ReservationRepository` for data persistence. It exposes the following public methods:\n\n- `ReservationDto createReservation(CreateReservationRequest request)`:\n    1. Validates the `CreateReservationRequest` to ensure all required fields are present and valid (e.g., future date, valid time, party size within limits).\n    2. Creates a new `Reservation` entity from the request, setting its initial status to `PENDING`.\n    3. Saves the `Reservation` entity using `reservationRepository.save()`.\n    4. Converts the saved `Reservation` entity to a `ReservationDto` and returns it.\n    5. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` if validation fails.\n\n- `ReservationDto getReservationById(Long id)`:\n    1. Retrieves a `Reservation` by its ID using `reservationRepository.findById()`.\n    2. If not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    3. Converts the `Reservation` entity to a `ReservationDto` and returns it.\n\n- `List<ReservationDto> getAllReservations()`:\n    1. Retrieves all `Reservation` entities using `reservationRepository.findAll()`.\n    2. Converts each `Reservation` entity to a `ReservationDto` and returns a list.\n\n- `List<ReservationDto> getReservationsByStatus(ReservationStatus status)`:\n    1. Retrieves `Reservation` entities filtered by `ReservationStatus` using a custom repository method `reservationRepository.findByStatus(status)`.\n    2. Converts each `Reservation` entity to a `ReservationDto` and returns a list.\n\n- `ReservationDto updateReservationStatus(Long id, ReservationStatus newStatus)`:\n    1. Retrieves the `Reservation` by ID using `reservationRepository.findById()`. If not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    2. Updates the status of the `Reservation` entity to `newStatus`.\n    3. Saves the updated `Reservation` entity using `reservationRepository.save()`.\n    4. Converts the updated `Reservation` entity to a `ReservationDto` and returns it.\n    5. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` if the status transition is invalid (e.g., trying to confirm an already cancelled reservation).\n\n- `void deleteReservation(Long id)`:\n    1. Retrieves the `Reservation` by ID using `reservationRepository.findById()`. If not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    2. Deletes the `Reservation` entity using `reservationRepository.deleteById()`.\n\n### Controller Layer\n\n`ReservationController.java` handles public-facing API endpoints for customers to create and view their own reservations. It injects `ReservationService`.\n\n- `POST /api/v1/reservations`:\n    - Accepts `CreateReservationRequest` in the request body.\n    - Calls `reservationService.createReservation()`.\n    - Returns `ReservationDto` with HTTP status 201 (Created).\n    - Returns HTTP status 400 (Bad Request) on `IllegalArgumentException`.\n\n- `GET /api/v1/reservations/{id}`:\n    - Retrieves a reservation by ID.\n    - Calls `reservationService.getReservationById()`.\n    - Returns `ReservationDto` with HTTP status 200 (OK).\n    - Returns HTTP status 404 (Not Found) on `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n\n`AdminReservationController.java` handles administrative API endpoints for viewing and managing all reservations. It injects `ReservationService`.\n\n- `GET /api/v1/admin/reservations`:\n    - Retrieves all reservations.\n    - Calls `reservationService.getAllReservations()`.\n    - Returns `List<ReservationDto>` with HTTP status 200 (OK).\n\n- `GET /api/v1/admin/reservations/status/{status}`:\n    - Retrieves reservations filtered by status.\n    - Calls `reservationService.getReservationsByStatus(status)`.\n    - Returns `List<ReservationDto>` with HTTP status 200 (OK).\n\n- `PUT /api/v1/admin/reservations/{id}/status`:\n    - Updates the status of a reservation.\n    - Accepts `ReservationStatus` as a request parameter.\n    - Calls `reservationService.updateReservationStatus()`.\n    - Returns `ReservationDto` with HTTP status 200 (OK).\n    - Returns HTTP status 400 (Bad Request) on `IllegalArgumentException`.\n    - Returns HTTP status 404 (Not Found) on `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n\n- `DELETE /api/v1/admin/reservations/{id}`:\n    - Deletes a reservation by ID.\n    - Calls `reservationService.deleteReservation()`.\n    - Returns HTTP status 204 (No Content).\n    - Returns HTTP status 404 (Not Found) on `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n\n### Data Transfer Objects\n\n`ReservationDto.java` is used for exposing reservation details in API responses. `CreateReservationRequest.java` is used to capture customer input when creating a new reservation.",
