  "feature_instruction": "The Payment Processing feature handles interactions with a third-party payment gateway (e.g., Razorpay) to facilitate online payments for orders. It consists of a `PaymentService` for core payment logic, a `PaymentController` for exposing API endpoints and handling webhooks, and several DTOs for request and response data.\n\n### PaymentService.java\nThis service is responsible for creating payment orders with the payment gateway and verifying payment signatures. It will expose the following public methods:\n\n1.  `createPaymentOrder(PaymentOrderRequest request, Long orderId, BigDecimal amount)`: This method takes a `PaymentOrderRequest` (though the current DTO is minimal, it's for future expansion), the `orderId` from the `order-management` feature, and the `amount` to be paid. It will:\n    a.  Construct a request payload for the payment gateway (e.g., Razorpay API) including the `amount`, `currency` (INR), and a unique `receipt` (e.g., `orderId`).\n    b.  Call the payment gateway's order creation API.\n    c.  Parse the response from the payment gateway to extract the `paymentOrderId` and other relevant details.\n    d.  Return a `PaymentResponse` DTO containing the `paymentOrderId`, `amount`, and `currency`.\n    e.  Throws `PaymentGatewayException` if the payment gateway call fails.\n\n2.  `verifyPaymentSignature(PaymentVerificationRequest request)`: This method takes a `PaymentVerificationRequest` which contains the payment gateway's order ID, payment ID, and signature. It will:\n    a.  Construct a payload for signature verification using the received details.\n    b.  Call the payment gateway's utility or API to verify the signature.\n    c.  Return `true` if the signature is valid, `false` otherwise.\n    d.  Throws `PaymentGatewayException` if the verification process encounters an error.\n\n### PaymentController.java\nThis controller exposes REST endpoints for initiating payments and handling payment gateway webhooks. It injects `PaymentService` and `OrderService` (from the `order-management` feature).\n\n1.  `createPaymentOrder(@RequestBody PaymentOrderRequest request)`: This endpoint (`POST /api/v1/payments/orders`) is called by the frontend to initiate a payment. It will:\n    a.  Call `paymentService.createPaymentOrder(request.getOrderId(), request.getAmount())`.\n    b.  Return a `ResponseEntity` with `PaymentResponse` and HTTP status 200 OK.\n    c.  If `PaymentGatewayException` is thrown, return `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 500 Internal Server Error and an appropriate error message.\n\n2.  `handlePaymentWebhook(@RequestBody PaymentVerificationRequest request)`: This endpoint (`POST /api/v1/payments/webhook`) is called by the payment gateway (e.g., Razorpay) to notify the application about payment status. It will:\n    a.  Call `paymentService.verifyPaymentSignature(request)`.\n    b.  If the signature is valid:\n        i.   Extract the `orderId` from the `request.getPaymentOrderId()` (assuming the `paymentOrderId` contains or can be mapped to the `orderId`).\n        ii.  Call `orderService.updateOrderStatus(orderId, OrderStatus.PAID)` to update the order status in the `order-management` feature.\n        iii. Return a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK and a success message.\n    c.  If the signature is invalid:\n        i.   Log the invalid signature attempt.\n        ii.  Return a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 400 Bad Request and an error message.\n    d.  If `PaymentGatewayException` is thrown during verification, return `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 500 Internal Server Error and an appropriate error message.\n\n### DTOs\n-   `PaymentOrderRequest.java`: Used for requesting a new payment order from the payment gateway. It will contain `orderId` and `amount`.\n-   `PaymentVerificationRequest.java`: Used for receiving payment verification details from the payment gateway webhook. It will contain `razorpay_order_id`, `razorpay_payment_id`, and `razorpay_signature`.\n-   `PaymentResponse.java`: Used for returning payment order details to the frontend after creating a payment order. It will contain `paymentOrderId`, `amount`, and `currency`.",
