{
  "feature_instruction": "The Event Management feature provides a complete backend solution for managing special events at Circuit House. It includes an `Event` entity to represent event details, an `EventRepository` for data persistence, an `EventService` for business logic, and two controllers: `EventController` for public access to event information and `AdminEventController` for administrative CRUD operations.\n\n### Event Entity (`Event.java`)\nThis JPA entity maps to the `events` table in the database. It includes fields such as `id`, `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `imageUrl`, and `active`. The `id` is a `Long` and serves as the primary key, auto-generated. `name` and `description` are `String` fields, with `name` being non-null and having a maximum length of 255 characters. `eventDate` is a `LocalDate`, `startTime` and `endTime` are `LocalTime`, and `imageUrl` is a `String` for the event's image URL. `active` is a `boolean` to indicate if the event is currently active or not.\n\n### Event DTO (`EventDto.java`)\nThis DTO is used for transferring event data between the controllers and services. It mirrors the `Event` entity but is designed for API exposure. It includes `id`, `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `imageUrl`, and `active`. All fields except `id` are mandatory for creation and updates, enforced by `@NotBlank` and `@NotNull` annotations.\n\n### Event Repository (`EventRepository.java`)\nThis interface extends `JpaRepository<Event, Long>`, providing standard CRUD operations. It includes a custom query method `findAllByActiveTrueOrderByEventDateAscStartTimeAsc()` to retrieve all active events, ordered by date and start time, for public display.\n\n### Event Service (`EventService.java`)\n`EventService` encapsulates the business logic for events. It injects `EventRepository` to interact with the database. All methods handle `EventDto` objects for input and output, converting them to and from `Event` entities internally.\n\n- `createEvent(EventDto eventDto)`: Creates a new event. It takes an `EventDto`, converts it to an `Event` entity, saves it via `EventRepository`, and returns the saved entity as an `EventDto`. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` if `eventDto` is null or invalid.\n- `updateEvent(Long id, EventDto eventDto)`: Updates an existing event. It finds the event by `id` using `EventRepository`. If found, it updates the fields from `eventDto`, saves the changes, and returns the updated `EventDto`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no event with the given `id` is found.\n- `getEventById(Long id)`: Retrieves an event by its ID. Returns an `EventDto` or throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found.\n- `getAllEvents()`: Retrieves all events, ordered by event date and start time. Returns a `List<EventDto>`.\n- `getAllActiveEvents()`: Retrieves all active events, ordered by event date and start time. Returns a `List<EventDto>`.\n- `deleteEvent(Long id)`: Deletes an event by its ID. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no event with the given `id` is found.\n\n### Event Controller (`EventController.java`)\nThis REST controller exposes public API endpoints for fetching event information. It injects `EventService`.\n\n- `getAllActiveEvents()`: Handles `GET /api/v1/events` to return a list of all active events. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<EventDto>>`.\n- `getEventById(Long id)`: Handles `GET /api/v1/events/{id}` to return a single event by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<EventDto>` or `404 NOT FOUND` if the event does not exist.\n\n### Admin Event Controller (`AdminEventController.java`)\nThis REST controller exposes admin-only API endpoints for CRUD operations on events. It injects `EventService` and requires administrator authentication.\n\n- `createEvent(EventDto eventDto)`: Handles `POST /api/v1/admin/events` to create a new event. Returns `ResponseEntity<EventDto>` with `201 CREATED` status.\n- `updateEvent(Long id, EventDto eventDto)`: Handles `PUT /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` to update an existing event. Returns `ResponseEntity<EventDto>` or `404 NOT FOUND` if the event does not exist.\n- `deleteEvent(Long id)`: Handles `DELETE /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` to delete an event. Returns `ResponseEntity<Void>` with `204 NO CONTENT` or `404 NOT FOUND`.\n- `getAllEvents()`: Handles `GET /api/v1/admin/events` to return a list of all events (active and inactive). Returns `ResponseEntity<List<EventDto>>`.\n- `getEventById(Long id)`: Handles `GET /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` to return a single event by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<EventDto>` or `404 NOT FOUND` if the event does not exist.\n\n### Error Handling\nBoth controllers will leverage a global exception handler (from `shared-backend` feature) to return consistent error responses for `ResourceNotFoundException` (HTTP 404) and `IllegalArgumentException` (HTTP 400).",
