{
  "feature_instruction": "The Testimonial Management feature provides a complete backend solution for handling customer testimonials for Circuit House. It includes a `Testimonial` entity for persistence, a `TestimonialRepository` for database interactions, a `TestimonialService` for business logic, and two controllers: `TestimonialController` for public access to approved testimonials, and `AdminTestimonialController` for administrative CRUD operations. A `TestimonialDto` is used for data transfer between layers.\n\n### Testimonial.java\nThis JPA entity maps to the `testimonials` table in the database. It will have fields for `id` (Long, primary key), `customerName` (String, not null, max 100 chars), `testimonialText` (String, not null, max 1000 chars), `rating` (Integer, not null, between 1 and 5), `approved` (Boolean, default false), and `createdAt` (LocalDateTime, auto-generated).\n\n### TestimonialRepository.java\nThis interface extends `JpaRepository<Testimonial, Long>` and provides standard CRUD operations. It will also include a custom query method `findByApprovedTrue()` to retrieve only approved testimonials.\n\n### TestimonialDto.java\nThis DTO will mirror the `Testimonial` entity but will be used for data transfer. It will include `id` (Long), `customerName` (String, with `@NotBlank` and `@Size` annotations), `testimonialText` (String, with `@NotBlank` and `@Size` annotations), `rating` (Integer, with `@NotNull` and `@Min`/`@Max` annotations), and `approved` (Boolean).\n\n### TestimonialService.java\nThis service class will encapsulate the business logic for testimonials. It will be injected with `TestimonialRepository`.\n\n**Public Functions:**\n\n1.  `TestimonialDto createTestimonial(TestimonialDto testimonialDto)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Map the `testimonialDto` to a `Testimonial` entity.\n        2.  Set `approved` to `false` by default for new testimonials.\n        3.  Set `createdAt` to `LocalDateTime.now()`.\n        4.  Save the `Testimonial` entity using `testimonialRepository.save()`.\n        5.  Map the saved entity back to a `TestimonialDto` and return it.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Throws `IllegalArgumentException` if `testimonialDto` is invalid.\n\n2.  `TestimonialDto getTestimonialById(Long id)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Retrieve the `Testimonial` entity by `id` using `testimonialRepository.findById()`.\n        2.  If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n        3.  Map the entity to a `TestimonialDto` and return it.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no testimonial with the given ID is found.\n\n3.  `List<TestimonialDto> getAllApprovedTestimonials()`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Retrieve all `Testimonial` entities where `approved` is `true` using `testimonialRepository.findByApprovedTrue()`.\n        2.  Map the list of entities to a list of `TestimonialDto` and return it.\n\n4.  `List<TestimonialDto> getAllTestimonials()`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Retrieve all `Testimonial` entities using `testimonialRepository.findAll()`.\n        2.  Map the list of entities to a list of `TestimonialDto` and return it.\n\n5.  `TestimonialDto updateTestimonial(Long id, TestimonialDto testimonialDto)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Retrieve the existing `Testimonial` entity by `id` using `testimonialRepository.findById()`.\n        2.  If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n        3.  Update the fields of the existing entity with values from `testimonialDto` (customerName, testimonialText, rating, approved).\n        4.  Save the updated `Testimonial` entity using `testimonialRepository.save()`.\n        5.  Map the saved entity back to a `TestimonialDto` and return it.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no testimonial with the given ID is found. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` if `testimonialDto` is invalid.\n\n6.  `void deleteTestimonial(Long id)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Check if a `Testimonial` with the given `id` exists using `testimonialRepository.existsById()`.\n        2.  If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n        3.  Delete the `Testimonial` entity by `id` using `testimonialRepository.deleteById()`.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no testimonial with the given ID is found.\n\n### TestimonialController.java\nThis controller exposes public endpoints for fetching approved testimonials. It will be injected with `TestimonialService`.\n\n**Public Functions:**\n\n1.  `ResponseEntity<List<TestimonialDto>> getAllApprovedTestimonials()`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.getAllApprovedTestimonials()`.\n        2.  Return the list of `TestimonialDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n\n### AdminTestimonialController.java\nThis controller exposes admin-only endpoints for CRUD operations on testimonials. It will be injected with `TestimonialService`.\n\n**Public Functions:**\n\n1.  `ResponseEntity<TestimonialDto> createTestimonial(@RequestBody TestimonialDto testimonialDto)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.createTestimonial(testimonialDto)`.\n        2.  Return the created `TestimonialDto` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Returns HTTP status 400 Bad Request if `testimonialDto` is invalid.\n\n2.  `ResponseEntity<TestimonialDto> getTestimonialById(@PathVariable Long id)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.getTestimonialById(id)`.\n        2.  Return the `TestimonialDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Returns HTTP status 404 Not Found if `ResourceNotFoundException` is thrown.\n\n3.  `ResponseEntity<List<TestimonialDto>> getAllTestimonials()`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.getAllTestimonials()`.\n        2.  Return the list of `TestimonialDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n\n4.  `ResponseEntity<TestimonialDto> updateTestimonial(@PathVariable Long id, @RequestBody TestimonialDto testimonialDto)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.updateTestimonial(id, testimonialDto)`.\n        2.  Return the updated `TestimonialDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Returns HTTP status 404 Not Found if `ResourceNotFoundException` is thrown. Returns HTTP status 400 Bad Request if `testimonialDto` is invalid.\n\n5.  `ResponseEntity<Void> deleteTestimonial(@PathVariable Long id)`:\n    *   **Logic:**\n        1.  Call `testimonialService.deleteTestimonial(id)`.\n        2.  Return HTTP status 204 No Content.\n    *   **Error Cases:** Returns HTTP status 404 Not Found if `ResourceNotFoundException` is thrown.",
