{
  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A202C] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#D69E2E] hover:bg-[#B7872A] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#D69E2E]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F7FAFC] (odd sections) / bg-white (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#2D3748] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides all static content pages and related components for the Circuit House restaurant, including the homepage, about page, contact page, gallery, loyalty program information, and an admin interface for managing customer testimonials. It integrates with the `menu-management`, `event-management`, and `testimonial-management` backend features to display dynamic content.\n\nThe `HomePage.tsx` serves as the landing page, composed of several key sections:\n1.  `HeroSection.tsx`: Displays a full-bleed hero image with a compelling headline and calls to action. It uses a restaurant-themed Unsplash image and an overlay for readability. The headline should be \"Experience Culinary Excellence at Circuit House\" and the subheadline \"Where Every Dish is a Masterpiece. Reserve Your Table Today.\"\n2.  `FeaturedMenuSection.tsx`: Showcases popular menu items. This component will utilize the `useMenu` hook to fetch a curated list of `MenuItemDto` objects from the `/api/v1/menu` endpoint of the `menu-management` feature. It should display at least three featured items, including their `name`, `description`, `price`, and `imageUrl`.\n3.  `TestimonialCarousel.tsx`: Presents customer testimonials in a rotating carousel. It uses the `useTestimonials` hook to fetch `TestimonialDto` objects from the `/api/v1/testimonials` endpoint of the `testimonial-management` feature. Each testimonial should display the `customerName` and `testimonialText`.\n4.  `EventsCtaSection.tsx`: A call-to-action section promoting upcoming events. This section will link to the `/events` page.\n\n`AboutPage.tsx` provides static content about the restaurant's story, mission, and ambiance, using descriptive and enticing copy.\n\n`ContactPage.tsx` displays contact information and includes a form and an embedded map:\n1.  `ContactInfo.tsx`: Renders the restaurant's address, phone number, email (placeholder: info@circuithouse.com), and opening hours (Mon-Sun: 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM).\n2.  `ContactForm.tsx`: A form for users to submit inquiries. This form will have fields for `name`, `email`, `subject`, and `message`. Upon submission, it should display a success or error message. This form does not interact with a backend API in this feature.\n3.  `GoogleMapEmbed.tsx`: Embeds a Google Map centered at the restaurant's coordinates (18.570737, 73.769986).\n\n`GalleryPage.tsx` will display a grid of high-quality images of the food and restaurant interior. The images should be placeholder Unsplash URLs relevant to a restaurant.\n\n`LoyaltyPage.tsx` explains the benefits and terms of the Circuit House loyalty program with confident and welcoming copy.\n\n`testimonial.ts` defines the TypeScript interface for `TestimonialDto`.\n\n`testimonialService.ts` provides the `getAllApprovedTestimonials`, `createTestimonial`, `getTestimonialById`, `updateTestimonial`, and `deleteTestimonial` functions for interacting with the `testimonial-management` backend. These functions will call the `/api/v1/testimonials` and `/api/v1/admin/testimonials` endpoints.\n\n`useTestimonials.ts` is a custom React Query hook that wraps `testimonialService.ts` functions to provide data fetching, caching, and mutation capabilities for testimonials. It exports `useGetAllApprovedTestimonials`, `useGetTestimonialById`, `useCreateTestimonial`, `useUpdateTestimonial`, and `useDeleteTestimonial`.\n\n`AdminTestimonialsPage.tsx` provides the administrative interface for managing testimonials. It uses `useTestimonials` to fetch all testimonials and orchestrates the `TestimonialsTable.tsx`, `TestimonialForm.tsx`, and `DeleteTestimonialDialog.tsx` components.\n\n`TestimonialsTable.tsx` displays a sortable and filterable table of testimonials, showing `customerName`, `testimonialText`, `rating`, and `approved` status. It includes action buttons to edit or delete a testimonial.\n\n`TestimonialForm.tsx` is a modal form used for creating or editing a testimonial. It takes an optional `TestimonialDto` prop for editing and includes fields for `customerName`, `testimonialText`, `rating`, and `approved` status. It uses `useCreateTestimonial` or `useUpdateTestimonial` from `useTestimonials.ts`.\n\n`DeleteTestimonialDialog.tsx` is a confirmation dialog for deleting a testimonial. It uses `useDeleteTestimonial` from `useTestimonials.ts`.\n\nAll pages (`HomePage.tsx`, `AboutPage.tsx`, `ContactPage.tsx`, `GalleryPage.tsx`, `LoyaltyPage.tsx`) that are public-facing must be wrapped in the `<Layout>` component from `@/components/Layout`. The `AdminTestimonialsPage.tsx` must be wrapped in `<AdminLayout>` from `@/components/AdminLayout`.\n",
