{
  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A202C] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#D69E2E] hover:bg-[#B77E00] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#D69E2E]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F7FAFC] (odd sections) / bg-white (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#2D3748] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides the frontend components and logic for displaying Circuit House's menu to customers and managing it via an admin interface. It consists of `menuService.ts` for API interactions, `useMenu.ts` for React Query hooks, `menu.ts` for type definitions, and several React components for both public display and admin management.\n\n### Public Menu Display (`MenuPage.tsx`, `MenuCategoryFilter.tsx`, `MenuItemGrid.tsx`, `MenuItemCard.tsx`)\n\nThe `MenuPage.tsx` serves as the main public-facing menu page. It uses the `useMenu` hook to fetch all available menu items. The page is structured with a prominent hero section, followed by a filterable menu display. It renders `MenuCategoryFilter.tsx` to allow users to filter menu items by category and `MenuItemGrid.tsx` to display the filtered items. Each item in the grid is rendered using `MenuItemCard.tsx`.\n\n- `MenuPage.tsx`:\n  - Fetches all available menu items using `useMenu.useGetAllMenuItems()`.\n  - Manages the active category filter state.\n  - Renders `MenuCategoryFilter` to allow users to select a category.\n  - Renders `MenuItemGrid` to display the filtered menu items.\n  - The hero section will feature a high-resolution image of Circuit House's interior or signature dishes, with a headline like \"Savor the Flavors of Circuit House\" and a subheadline \"An elegant dining experience awaits.\"\n\n- `MenuCategoryFilter.tsx`:\n  - Receives `categories: string[]` and `onSelectCategory: (category: string | null) => void` as props.\n  - Displays buttons for each unique category (e.g., \"Appetizers\", \"Main Courses\", \"Desserts\") and an \"All\" option.\n  - When a category button is clicked, it calls `onSelectCategory` with the selected category name or `null` for \"All\".\n\n- `MenuItemGrid.tsx`:\n  - Receives `menuItems: MenuItemDto[]` as a prop.\n  - Renders a responsive grid of `MenuItemCard` components, passing each `MenuItemDto` to a card.\n\n- `MenuItemCard.tsx`:\n  - Receives `menuItem: MenuItemDto` as a prop.\n  - Displays the `menuItem.imageUrl`, `menuItem.name`, `menuItem.description`, and `menuItem.price` in an elegant card format.\n\n### Admin Menu Management (`AdminMenuPage.tsx`, `MenuTable.tsx`, `MenuItemForm.tsx`, `DeleteMenuItemDialog.tsx`)\n\n`AdminMenuPage.tsx` provides the interface for administrators to manage menu items. It uses `useMenu` to fetch, create, update, and delete menu items. It orchestrates the display of `MenuTable.tsx` for listing items, `MenuItemForm.tsx` for adding/editing, and `DeleteMenuItemDialog.tsx` for confirmation.\n\n- `AdminMenuPage.tsx`:\n  - Fetches all menu items using `useMenu.useGetAllMenuItemsAdmin()`.\n  - Provides functions to open `MenuItemForm` for creating or editing items, and `DeleteMenuItemDialog` for deleting items.\n  - Uses `useMenu.useCreateMenuItem()`, `useMenu.useUpdateMenuItem()`, and `useMenu.useDeleteMenuItem()` for mutations.\n  - Renders `MenuTable` to display all menu items.\n  - Renders `MenuItemForm` in a modal/dialog for creating or editing a `MenuItemDto`.\n  - Renders `DeleteMenuItemDialog` in a modal/dialog for confirming deletion of a menu item by `id`.\n\n- `MenuTable.tsx`:\n  - Receives `menuItems: MenuItemDto[]`, `onEdit: (item: MenuItemDto) => void`, and `onDelete: (id: Long) => void` as props.\n  - Displays a data table of menu items with columns for name, category, price, availability, and actions (Edit, Delete).\n  - Calls `onEdit` when the Edit button is clicked for a specific item.\n  - Calls `onDelete` when the Delete button is clicked for a specific item.\n\n- `MenuItemForm.tsx`:\n  - Receives `menuItem?: MenuItemDto` (optional, for editing), `onClose: () => void`, and `onSubmit: (item: MenuItemDto) => void` as props.\n  - Provides a form with fields for `name`, `description`, `price`, `category`, `imageUrl`, and `available`.\n  - Submits the form data as a `MenuItemDto` to `onSubmit`.\n  - Calls `onClose` upon successful submission or cancellation.\n\n- `DeleteMenuItemDialog.tsx`:\n  - Receives `menuItemId: Long`, `onClose: () => void`, and `onConfirm: (id: Long) => void` as props.\n  - Displays a confirmation message for deleting the menu item.\n  - Calls `onConfirm` when the user confirms deletion.\n  - Calls `onClose` upon confirmation or cancellation.\n\n### Data Flow and API Interactions\n\n1.  **`menu.ts`**: Defines the `MenuItemDto` interface, which mirrors the backend `MenuItemDto` data shape.\n    ```

typescript\n    export interface MenuItemDto {\n      id: number;\n      name: string;\n      description: string;\n      price: number;\n      category: string; // e.g., \"Appetizers\", \"Main Course\", \"Desserts\"\n      imageUrl: string;\n      available: boolean;\n    }\n    

```\n\n2.  **`menuService.ts`**: Encapsulates all direct API calls to the `menu-management` backend feature.\n    - `getAllMenuItems()`: Calls `GET /api/v1/menu` to fetch all publicly available menu items.\n    - `getMenuItemById(id: number)`: Calls `GET /api/v1/menu/{id}` to fetch a single menu item.\n    - `getAllMenuItemsAdmin()`: Calls `GET /api/v1/admin/menu` to fetch all menu items for admin.\n    - `createMenuItem(item: MenuItemDto)`: Calls `POST /api/v1/admin/menu` to create a new menu item.\n    - `updateMenuItem(id: number, item: MenuItemDto)`: Calls `PUT /api/v1/admin/menu/{id}` to update an existing menu item.\n    - `deleteMenuItem(id: number)`: Calls `DELETE /api/v1/admin/menu/{id}` to delete a menu item.\n\n3.  **`useMenu.ts`**: Provides React Query hooks that wrap the `menuService` functions, handling caching, loading states, and mutations.\n    - `useGetAllMenuItems()`: Uses `menuService.getAllMenuItems()` for public display.\n    - `useGetMenuItemById(id: number)`: Uses `menuService.getMenuItemById()`.\n    - `useGetAllMenuItemsAdmin()`: Uses `menuService.getAllMenuItemsAdmin()` for admin display.\n    - `useCreateMenuItem()`: Provides a mutation hook for `menuService.createMenuItem()`.\n    - `useUpdateMenuItem()`: Provides a mutation hook for `menuService.updateMenuItem()`.\n    - `useDeleteMenuItem()`: Provides a mutation hook for `menuService.deleteMenuItem()`.\n\n### Error Handling\n\nAll API calls in `menuService.ts` should include basic error handling, logging errors to the console. The React Query hooks in `useMenu.ts` will expose error states to the components, allowing for user-friendly error messages or fallback UI.\n",
