{
  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A202C] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#D69E2E] hover:bg-[#c28b29] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#D69E2E]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F7FAFC] (odd sections) / bg-white (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#2D3748] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides both public-facing event listings and an administrative interface for managing events at Circuit House. It consists of `event.ts` for defining the data structure, `eventService.ts` for API interactions, `useEvents.ts` as a React Query hook, and several React components and pages for display and management.\n\n### Data Structures (`event.ts`)\nThe `event.ts` file defines the `EventDto` interface, which mirrors the `EventDto` data shape from the `event-management` backend feature. This ensures type safety and consistency across the frontend.\n\n```

typescript\nexport interface EventDto {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  eventDate: string; // LocalDate from backend, use string for simplicity in frontend\n  startTime: string; // LocalTime from backend, use string\n  endTime: string; // LocalTime from backend, use string\n  imageUrl: string;\n  active: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface CreateEventDto {\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  eventDate: string;\n  startTime: string;\n  endTime: string;\n  imageUrl: string;\n  active: boolean;\n}\n

```\n\n### API Service (`eventService.ts`)\nThe `eventService.ts` file encapsulates all direct API calls to the `event-management` backend. It uses `axios` (via `apiClient`) to perform HTTP requests. All functions return `Promise<EventDto[]>` or `Promise<EventDto>` or `Promise<void>`.\n\n- `getAllActiveEvents(): Promise<EventDto[]>`: Fetches all active events for public display.\n- `getAllEvents(): Promise<EventDto[]>`: Fetches all events (active and inactive) for admin display.\n- `getEventById(id: number): Promise<EventDto>`: Fetches a single event by its ID.\n- `createEvent(event: CreateEventDto): Promise<EventDto>`: Sends a POST request to create a new event.\n- `updateEvent(id: number, event: CreateEventDto): Promise<EventDto>`: Sends a PUT request to update an existing event.\n- `deleteEvent(id: number): Promise<void>`: Sends a DELETE request to remove an event.\n\n### React Query Hook (`useEvents.ts`)\nThe `useEvents.ts` hook leverages `react-query` to provide data fetching, caching, and mutation capabilities for events. It exports the following custom hooks:\n\n- `useGetAllActiveEvents()`: Uses `eventService.getAllActiveEvents` to fetch and cache active events. Returns `UseQueryResult<EventDto[], Error>`.\n- `useGetAllEvents()`: Uses `eventService.getAllEvents` to fetch and cache all events (for admin). Returns `UseQueryResult<EventDto[], Error>`.\n- `useGetEventById(id: number)`: Uses `eventService.getEventById` to fetch a single event. Returns `UseQueryResult<EventDto, Error>`.\n- `useCreateEvent()`: Provides a mutation function to create an event using `eventService.createEvent`. On success, it invalidates the `['events']` query to refetch the event list. Returns `UseMutationResult<EventDto, Error, CreateEventDto>`.\n- `useUpdateEvent()`: Provides a mutation function to update an event using `eventService.updateEvent`. On success, it invalidates the `['events']` query. Returns `UseMutationResult<EventDto, Error, { id: number; event: CreateEventDto }>`.\n- `useDeleteEvent()`: Provides a mutation function to delete an event using `eventService.deleteEvent`. On success, it invalidates the `['events']` query. Returns `UseMutationResult<void, Error, number>`.\n\n### Public Event Listing Page (`EventsPage.tsx`)\n`EventsPage.tsx` is the public-facing page that displays a list of upcoming and past events. It uses the `Layout` component from `core-ui` for consistent navigation and footer.\n\n- It fetches active events using `useGetAllActiveEvents()`.\n- It renders the `EventList` component, passing the fetched events as props.\n- The page structure includes a hero section with a background image (Unsplash URL for restaurant/food), a compelling headline, and a subheadline. Below the hero, it displays the event list.\n\n### Event List Component (`EventList.tsx`)\n`EventList.tsx` is a presentational component that receives an array of `EventDto` objects and renders them as a grid of event cards.\n\n- Each event card displays the event's `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, and `imageUrl`.\n- The layout should be responsive, displaying events in a grid format.\n\n### Admin Event Management Page (`AdminEventsPage.tsx`)\n`AdminEventsPage.tsx` provides the administrative interface for managing events. It uses the `AdminLayout` component from `core-ui` for consistent admin navigation.\n\n- It fetches all events (active and inactive) using `useGetAllEvents()`.\n- It provides functionality to open `EventForm` for creating or editing an event and `DeleteEventDialog` for confirming deletion.\n- The page renders `EventsTable` to display the list of events.\n\n### Events Table Component (`EventsTable.tsx`)\n`EventsTable.tsx` displays a tabular list of events with options to edit or delete each event. It receives `EventDto[]`, `onEdit` and `onDelete` callbacks as props.\n\n- Each row in the table represents an event and includes its `name`, `eventDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, and `active` status.\n- Action buttons (Edit, Delete) are provided for each event, triggering the `onEdit` and `onDelete` callbacks.\n\n### Event Form Component (`EventForm.tsx`)\n`EventForm.tsx` is a reusable form component for creating or editing event details. It can be rendered within a dialog or modal.\n\n- It accepts an optional `event` prop (of type `EventDto`) for pre-filling the form fields in edit mode.\n- It includes input fields for `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `imageUrl`, and `active` status.\n- It uses `react-hook-form` and `yup` for form validation.\n- On submission, it calls the appropriate `useCreateEvent` or `useUpdateEvent` mutation from `useEvents.ts`.\n\n### Delete Event Dialog Component (`DeleteEventDialog.tsx`)\n`DeleteEventDialog.tsx` is a confirmation dialog for deleting an event.\n\n- It receives `eventId` and `onClose` callback as props.\n- When confirmed, it calls the `useDeleteEvent` mutation from `useEvents.ts` to delete the specified event.\n\n### Inter-file Wiring\n- `EventsPage.tsx` imports and uses `useEvents.ts` and `EventList.tsx`.\n- `AdminEventsPage.tsx` imports and uses `useEvents.ts`, `EventsTable.tsx`, `EventForm.tsx`, and `DeleteEventDialog.tsx`.\n- `useEvents.ts` imports and uses `eventService.ts` and `event.ts`.\n- `eventService.ts` imports and uses `event.ts`.\n- `EventList.tsx` imports `event.ts`.\n- `EventsTable.tsx` imports `event.ts`.\n- `EventForm.tsx` imports `event.ts`.\n\n### Cross-Feature Contracts\n- This feature consumes the `event-management` backend feature's API endpoints for events. Specifically:\n  - `GET /api/v1/events` for `getAllActiveEvents`\n  - `GET /api/v1/admin/events` for `getAllEvents`\n  - `GET /api/v1/events/{id}` and `GET /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` for `getEventById`\n  - `POST /api/v1/admin/events` for `createEvent`\n  - `PUT /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` for `updateEvent`\n  - `DELETE /api/v1/admin/events/{id}` for `deleteEvent`\n- It uses `Layout` and `AdminLayout` components from the `core-ui` feature.\n- It relies on the authentication context (implicitly via `AdminLayout` and protected routes) from the `authentication` feature to secure admin routes.",
